---
args: { quoteCase: CustomQuoteProposalCase }
returns: CustomQuoteProposal
---
1. Bind measurements = qualifyShopMeasurements(quoteCase.customerRequirements, quoteCase.measurements). An approximate customer dimension without a verified tolerance remains a provisional assumption, not a production value.
2. Bind concept = selectFabricationConcept(quoteCase.selectedConceptId, quoteCase.concepts, measurements, quoteCase.finishReferences, quoteCase.acceptedSamples). Refuse concepts whose features lack accepted measurements or whose physical finish reference is not accepted.
3. Bind route = matchCertifiedShopRoute(concept, quoteCase.equipment, quoteCase.certificateRequirements). If the shop lacks a required certification, disclose that gap and route specialist work; never imply the shop can certify itself.
4. Bind pricing = validateMaterialPricing(quoteCase.materials, quoteCase.designRevisions, route). A change to design tooling revises both route and cost. Expired material prices cannot support a committed quote.
5. Return { caseId: quoteCase.caseId, selectedConceptId: quoteCase.selectedConceptId, feasibility: { missingMeasurements: measurements.missingMeasurements, conceptBlockers: concept.blockers, capabilityGaps: route.capabilityGaps, finishAcceptanceGaps: concept.finishAcceptanceGaps, certificationGaps: route.certificationGaps, expiredMaterialIds: pricing.expiredMaterialIds, provisional: measurements.missingMeasurements.length > 0 || route.capabilityGaps.length > 0 || pricing.expiredMaterialIds.length > 0 }, productionRoute: route.steps, materialCostBasis: pricing.costBasis, toolingCostChanges: pricing.toolingChanges, quoteExpiry: pricing.earliestExpiry, quoteStatus: measurements.missingMeasurements.length > 0 || route.capabilityGaps.length > 0 || pricing.expiredMaterialIds.length > 0 ? "provisional" : "review-required", scopeConfirmation: concept.blockers, commitAllowed: false }.
